        ['A sample of gas occupies 500 cm³ at 15 °C and 750 mmHg. (a) State the general gas law. (b) Calculate its volume at s.t.p. (c) State two assumptions of the kinetic theory of gases.', ['Combined gas law', 'Convert to kelvin', 'V at s.t.p. 467.7', 'Two assumptions'], '(a) P₁V₁/T₁ = P₂V₂/T₂ for a fixed mass of gas. (b) T₁ = 288 K; V₂ = 750 × 500 × 273 ÷ (760 × 288) = 467.7 cm³. (c) Any two: gas molecules are in constant random motion; the volume of the molecules is negligible compared with the volume of the container; there are no forces of attraction between molecules; collisions are perfectly elastic; average kinetic energy is proportional to absolute temperature.', 'Compare your answer with the model answer and tick off the points you made.', 4, 'theory', 8],
        ['A sample of gas occupies 250 cm³ at 15 °C and 760 mmHg. (a) State the general gas law. (b) Calculate its volume at s.t.p. (c) State two assumptions of the kinetic theory of gases.', ['Combined gas law', 'Convert to kelvin', 'V at s.t.p. 237', 'Two assumptions'], '(a) P₁V₁/T₁ = P₂V₂/T₂ for a fixed mass of gas. (b) T₁ = 288 K; V₂ = 760 × 250 × 273 ÷ (760 × 288) = 237 cm³. (c) Any two: gas molecules are in constant random motion; the volume of the molecules is negligible compared with the volume of the container; there are no forces of attraction between molecules; collisions are perfectly elastic; average kinetic energy is proportional to absolute temperature.', 'Compare your answer with the model answer and tick off the points you made.', 4, 'theory', 8],
        ['A sample of gas occupies 250 cm³ at 27 °C and 760 mmHg. (a) State the general gas law. (b) Calculate its volume at s.t.p. (c) State two assumptions of the kinetic theory of gases.', ['Combined gas law', 'Convert to kelvin', 'V at s.t.p. 227.5', 'Two assumptions'], '(a) P₁V₁/T₁ = P₂V₂/T₂ for a fixed mass of gas. (b) T₁ = 300 K; V₂ = 760 × 250 × 273 ÷ (760 × 300) = 227.5 cm³. (c) Any two: gas molecules are in constant random motion; the volume of the molecules is negligible compared with the volume of the container; there are no forces of attraction between molecules; collisions are perfectly elastic; average kinetic energy is proportional to absolute temperature.', 'Compare your answer with the model answer and tick off the points you made.', 4, 'theory', 8],
        ['A sample of gas occupies 300 cm³ at 15 °C and 750 mmHg. (a) State the general gas law. (b) Calculate its volume at s.t.p. (c) State two assumptions of the kinetic theory of gases.', ['Combined gas law', 'Convert to kelvin', 'V at s.t.p. 280.6', 'Two assumptions'], '(a) P₁V₁/T₁ = P₂V₂/T₂ for a fixed mass of gas. (b) T₁ = 288 K; V₂ = 750 × 300 × 273 ÷ (760 × 288) = 280.6 cm³. (c) Any two: gas molecules are in constant random motion; the volume of the molecules is negligible compared with the volume of the container; there are no forces of attraction between molecules; collisions are perfectly elastic; average kinetic energy is proportional to absolute temperature.', 'Compare your answer with the model answer and tick off the points you made.', 4, 'theory', 8],
        ['A sample of gas occupies 200 cm³ at 27 °C and 760 mmHg. (a) State the general gas law. (b) Calculate its volume at s.t.p. (c) State two assumptions of the kinetic theory of gases.', ['Combined gas law', 'Convert to kelvin', 'V at s.t.p. 182', 'Two assumptions'], '(a) P₁V₁/T₁ = P₂V₂/T₂ for a fixed mass of gas. (b) T₁ = 300 K; V₂ = 760 × 200 × 273 ÷ (760 × 300) = 182 cm³. (c) Any two: gas molecules are in constant random motion; the volume of the molecules is negligible compared with the volume of the container; there are no forces of attraction between molecules; collisions are perfectly elastic; average kinetic energy is proportional to absolute temperature.', 'Compare your answer with the model answer and tick off the points you made.', 4, 'theory', 8],
