        ['5.3 g of anhydrous sodium carbonate was dissolved in water and made up to 250 cm³. 25.0 cm³ of this solution required 25 cm³ of hydrochloric acid for neutralisation using methyl orange. Na₂CO₃ + 2HCl → 2NaCl + H₂O + CO₂ (Na₂CO₃ = 106) Calculate (a) the concentration of Na₂CO₃ in mol/dm³, (b) the moles of Na₂CO₃ in 25.0 cm³, (c) the concentration of HCl in mol/dm³, (d) the concentration of HCl in g/dm³ (HCl = 36.5).', ['Molar concentration of Na₂CO₃', 'Moles in 25 cm³', 'Mole ratio 1 : 2', 'HCl mol/dm³', 'HCl g/dm³'], '(a) Moles Na₂CO₃ = 5.3 ÷ 106 = 0.05 mol in 250 cm³, so c = 0.05 × 4 = 0.2 mol/dm³. (b) n = 0.2 × 25.0 ÷ 1000 = 0.005 mol. (c) Moles HCl = 2 × 0.005 = 0.01 mol; c = 0.01 ÷ 0.025 = 0.4 mol/dm³. (d) 0.4 × 36.5 = 14.6 g/dm³.', 'Compare your answer with the model answer and tick off the points you made.', 5, 'theory', 10],
        ['10.6 g of anhydrous sodium carbonate was dissolved in water and made up to 250 cm³. 25.0 cm³ of this solution required 25 cm³ of hydrochloric acid for neutralisation using methyl orange. Na₂CO₃ + 2HCl → 2NaCl + H₂O + CO₂ (Na₂CO₃ = 106) Calculate (a) the concentration of Na₂CO₃ in mol/dm³, (b) the moles of Na₂CO₃ in 25.0 cm³, (c) the concentration of HCl in mol/dm³, (d) the concentration of HCl in g/dm³ (HCl = 36.5).', ['Molar concentration of Na₂CO₃', 'Moles in 25 cm³', 'Mole ratio 1 : 2', 'HCl mol/dm³', 'HCl g/dm³'], '(a) Moles Na₂CO₃ = 10.6 ÷ 106 = 0.1 mol in 250 cm³, so c = 0.1 × 4 = 0.4 mol/dm³. (b) n = 0.4 × 25.0 ÷ 1000 = 0.01 mol. (c) Moles HCl = 2 × 0.01 = 0.02 mol; c = 0.02 ÷ 0.025 = 0.8 mol/dm³. (d) 0.8 × 36.5 = 29.2 g/dm³.', 'Compare your answer with the model answer and tick off the points you made.', 5, 'theory', 10],
        ['5.3 g of anhydrous sodium carbonate was dissolved in water and made up to 250 cm³. 25.0 cm³ of this solution required 20 cm³ of hydrochloric acid for neutralisation using methyl orange. Na₂CO₃ + 2HCl → 2NaCl + H₂O + CO₂ (Na₂CO₃ = 106) Calculate (a) the concentration of Na₂CO₃ in mol/dm³, (b) the moles of Na₂CO₃ in 25.0 cm³, (c) the concentration of HCl in mol/dm³, (d) the concentration of HCl in g/dm³ (HCl = 36.5).', ['Molar concentration of Na₂CO₃', 'Moles in 25 cm³', 'Mole ratio 1 : 2', 'HCl mol/dm³', 'HCl g/dm³'], '(a) Moles Na₂CO₃ = 5.3 ÷ 106 = 0.05 mol in 250 cm³, so c = 0.05 × 4 = 0.2 mol/dm³. (b) n = 0.2 × 25.0 ÷ 1000 = 0.005 mol. (c) Moles HCl = 2 × 0.005 = 0.01 mol; c = 0.01 ÷ 0.02 = 0.5 mol/dm³. (d) 0.5 × 36.5 = 18.25 g/dm³.', 'Compare your answer with the model answer and tick off the points you made.', 5, 'theory', 10],
        ['5.3 g of anhydrous sodium carbonate was dissolved in water and made up to 250 cm³. 25.0 cm³ of this solution required 22 cm³ of hydrochloric acid for neutralisation using methyl orange. Na₂CO₃ + 2HCl → 2NaCl + H₂O + CO₂ (Na₂CO₃ = 106) Calculate (a) the concentration of Na₂CO₃ in mol/dm³, (b) the moles of Na₂CO₃ in 25.0 cm³, (c) the concentration of HCl in mol/dm³, (d) the concentration of HCl in g/dm³ (HCl = 36.5).', ['Molar concentration of Na₂CO₃', 'Moles in 25 cm³', 'Mole ratio 1 : 2', 'HCl mol/dm³', 'HCl g/dm³'], '(a) Moles Na₂CO₃ = 5.3 ÷ 106 = 0.05 mol in 250 cm³, so c = 0.05 × 4 = 0.2 mol/dm³. (b) n = 0.2 × 25.0 ÷ 1000 = 0.005 mol. (c) Moles HCl = 2 × 0.005 = 0.01 mol; c = 0.01 ÷ 0.022 = 0.4545 mol/dm³. (d) 0.4545 × 36.5 = 16.59 g/dm³.', 'Compare your answer with the model answer and tick off the points you made.', 5, 'theory', 10],
        ['2.65 g of anhydrous sodium carbonate was dissolved in water and made up to 250 cm³. 25.0 cm³ of this solution required 25 cm³ of hydrochloric acid for neutralisation using methyl orange. Na₂CO₃ + 2HCl → 2NaCl + H₂O + CO₂ (Na₂CO₃ = 106) Calculate (a) the concentration of Na₂CO₃ in mol/dm³, (b) the moles of Na₂CO₃ in 25.0 cm³, (c) the concentration of HCl in mol/dm³, (d) the concentration of HCl in g/dm³ (HCl = 36.5).', ['Molar concentration of Na₂CO₃', 'Moles in 25 cm³', 'Mole ratio 1 : 2', 'HCl mol/dm³', 'HCl g/dm³'], '(a) Moles Na₂CO₃ = 2.65 ÷ 106 = 0.025 mol in 250 cm³, so c = 0.025 × 4 = 0.1 mol/dm³. (b) n = 0.1 × 25.0 ÷ 1000 = 0.0025 mol. (c) Moles HCl = 2 × 0.0025 = 0.005 mol; c = 0.005 ÷ 0.025 = 0.2 mol/dm³. (d) 0.2 × 36.5 = 7.3 g/dm³.', 'Compare your answer with the model answer and tick off the points you made.', 5, 'theory', 10],
