        ['The pH of a solution with [H⁺] = 10⁻² mol/dm³ is ___.', ['2'], '', 'pH = −log 10⁻².', 2, 'fill'],
        ['Ethanoic acid, CH₃COOH, has Ka = 1.6 × 10⁻⁵ mol/dm³ at 25 °C. For a 0.05 mol/dm³ solution: (a) write the expression for Ka, (b) calculate [H⁺], (c) calculate the pH, (d) calculate the percentage ionisation. (e) Explain why this acid is described as weak.', ['Ka expression', '[H⁺] value', 'pH 3.05', 'Percentage ionisation', 'Partial ionisation'], '(a) Ka = [H⁺][CH₃COO⁻] ÷ [CH₃COOH]. (b) Since [H⁺] = [CH₃COO⁻] and ionisation is small, [H⁺]² = Ka × c, so [H⁺] = √(1.6 × 10⁻⁵ × 0.05) = 8.94 × 10⁻⁴ mol/dm³. (c) pH = −log(8.94 × 10⁻⁴) = 3.05. (d) % ionisation = 8.94 × 10⁻⁴ ÷ 0.05 × 100 = 1.79%. (e) Only a small fraction of its molecules ionise in water.', 'Compare your answer with the model answer and tick off the points you made.', 5, 'theory', 10],
        ['Ethanoic acid, CH₃COOH, has Ka = 1 × 10⁻⁵ mol/dm³ at 25 °C. For a 0.05 mol/dm³ solution: (a) write the expression for Ka, (b) calculate [H⁺], (c) calculate the pH, (d) calculate the percentage ionisation. (e) Explain why this acid is described as weak.', ['Ka expression', '[H⁺] value', 'pH 3.15', 'Percentage ionisation', 'Partial ionisation'], '(a) Ka = [H⁺][CH₃COO⁻] ÷ [CH₃COOH]. (b) Since [H⁺] = [CH₃COO⁻] and ionisation is small, [H⁺]² = Ka × c, so [H⁺] = √(1 × 10⁻⁵ × 0.05) = 7.07 × 10⁻⁴ mol/dm³. (c) pH = −log(7.07 × 10⁻⁴) = 3.15. (d) % ionisation = 7.07 × 10⁻⁴ ÷ 0.05 × 100 = 1.41%. (e) Only a small fraction of its molecules ionise in water.', 'Compare your answer with the model answer and tick off the points you made.', 5, 'theory', 10],
        ['Ethanoic acid, CH₃COOH, has Ka = 1.6 × 10⁻⁵ mol/dm³ at 25 °C. For a 0.1 mol/dm³ solution: (a) write the expression for Ka, (b) calculate [H⁺], (c) calculate the pH, (d) calculate the percentage ionisation. (e) Explain why this acid is described as weak.', ['Ka expression', '[H⁺] value', 'pH 2.90', 'Percentage ionisation', 'Partial ionisation'], '(a) Ka = [H⁺][CH₃COO⁻] ÷ [CH₃COOH]. (b) Since [H⁺] = [CH₃COO⁻] and ionisation is small, [H⁺]² = Ka × c, so [H⁺] = √(1.6 × 10⁻⁵ × 0.1) = 1.26 × 10⁻³ mol/dm³. (c) pH = −log(1.26 × 10⁻³) = 2.90. (d) % ionisation = 1.26 × 10⁻³ ÷ 0.1 × 100 = 1.26%. (e) Only a small fraction of its molecules ionise in water.', 'Compare your answer with the model answer and tick off the points you made.', 5, 'theory', 10],
        ['Ethanoic acid, CH₃COOH, has Ka = 1.8 × 10⁻⁵ mol/dm³ at 25 °C. For a 0.2 mol/dm³ solution: (a) write the expression for Ka, (b) calculate [H⁺], (c) calculate the pH, (d) calculate the percentage ionisation. (e) Explain why this acid is described as weak.', ['Ka expression', '[H⁺] value', 'pH 2.72', 'Percentage ionisation', 'Partial ionisation'], '(a) Ka = [H⁺][CH₃COO⁻] ÷ [CH₃COOH]. (b) Since [H⁺] = [CH₃COO⁻] and ionisation is small, [H⁺]² = Ka × c, so [H⁺] = √(1.8 × 10⁻⁵ × 0.2) = 1.9 × 10⁻³ mol/dm³. (c) pH = −log(1.9 × 10⁻³) = 2.72. (d) % ionisation = 1.9 × 10⁻³ ÷ 0.2 × 100 = 0.95%. (e) Only a small fraction of its molecules ionise in water.', 'Compare your answer with the model answer and tick off the points you made.', 5, 'theory', 10],
        ['Ethanoic acid, CH₃COOH, has Ka = 1 × 10⁻⁵ mol/dm³ at 25 °C. For a 0.2 mol/dm³ solution: (a) write the expression for Ka, (b) calculate [H⁺], (c) calculate the pH, (d) calculate the percentage ionisation. (e) Explain why this acid is described as weak.', ['Ka expression', '[H⁺] value', 'pH 2.85', 'Percentage ionisation', 'Partial ionisation'], '(a) Ka = [H⁺][CH₃COO⁻] ÷ [CH₃COOH]. (b) Since [H⁺] = [CH₃COO⁻] and ionisation is small, [H⁺]² = Ka × c, so [H⁺] = √(1 × 10⁻⁵ × 0.2) = 1.41 × 10⁻³ mol/dm³. (c) pH = −log(1.41 × 10⁻³) = 2.85. (d) % ionisation = 1.41 × 10⁻³ ÷ 0.2 × 100 = 0.71%. (e) Only a small fraction of its molecules ionise in water.', 'Compare your answer with the model answer and tick off the points you made.', 5, 'theory', 10],
